  "answer_text": "**wakehealth.edu** is the official website for **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist** (formerly known as Wake Forest Baptist Health), a prominent, nationally recognized academic medical center and health system based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina. \n\nThe website serves as a central hub for patients, students, researchers, and healthcare professionals. Here is an overview of what you can find and do on the site:\n\n### 1. Patient Care & Services\n* **Find a Doctor & Locations:** Patients can search for primary care providers, specialists, and clinical locations across northwest North Carolina and southwest Virginia.\n* **Patient Portal (MyAtriumHealth):** The website provides access to the patient portal (formerly *MyWakeHealth*, now integrated into **MyAtriumHealth**), where patients can schedule appointments, message their doctors, view test results, and pay medical bills.\n* **Specialty Care:** Information on world-class medical services, including the NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, Brenner Children\u2019s Hospital, heart and vascular care, orthopedics, and neurosciences.\n\n### 2. Education & Academics\n* **Wake Forest University School of Medicine:** The site hosts information for the medical school, which is the academic core of the health system. It provides resources for prospective medical students, PA (physician assistant) students, nurse anesthesia students, and those seeking residency or fellowship programs.\n\n### 3. Research & Innovation\n* **Clinical Trials:** Patients and physicians can search for active clinical trials and research studies being conducted at Wake Forest.\n* **Biomedical Research:** Information on groundbreaking research in areas such as aging, Alzheimer's, cancer, and regenerative medicine.\n\n### Recent Organizational Changes\n* **Atrium Health Merger:** In 2021, Wake Forest Baptist Health strategically combined with Charlotte-based Atrium Health, rebranding as **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist**.\n* **Advocate Health:** Atrium Health subsequently merged with Advocate Aurora Health to form **Advocate Health**, which is one of the largest non-profit health systems in the United States. Despite these mergers, `wakehealth.edu` remains the primary academic and regional clinical portal for the Winston-Salem and Winston-Salem-adjacent service areas.",
